WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.930
<b>The Day of the Verdict</b>

3
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.860
Franky! Hold on!

4
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.560
For what?

5
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.460
For your pants, you silly boy!

6
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.030
I swear, you'd think after
all that attention you got

7
00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.270
last time you went out

8
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.060
dressed like that, you'd be
wise enough to not do it again.

9
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.760
Geez. I'm just goin'
out to get a few things.

10
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.410
<b>Mr. Tom</b>

11
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.700
Now, that you're dressed,
you can skedaddle!

12
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.980
Thanks. I can't believe
she's makin' a big dinner

13
00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.990
just cause the stupid judge is
finally sayin' Tom's not guilty.

14
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.830
He never was in the first place.

15
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.630
Alright.

16
00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.440
Rise and shine!
Tom! Iceburg! Get up!

17
00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.140
Today's judgment day!

18
00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.640
Don't wanna sleep
through your big trial!

19
00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.710
Let's get down to the harbor!

20
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.850
They're gonna hand down Tom's sentence!

21
00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.100
The spectators are boarding the ship in
droves.

22
00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.140
The people are really interested.

23
00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.040
Seems like it'll be a big trial.

24
00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.320
Have you had a chance to see
the sea train yet, your honor?

25
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.380
I have indeed. Quite impressive.
A true feat of ingenuity.

26
00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.310
He fulfilled his end of the bargain.

27
00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.550
I'm certain the
people will rejoice

28
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.080
to see their hero go free.

29
00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.080
Is Tom here yet?

30
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.310
I wish it would start already.

31
00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.840
Come on! We gotta hurry
before all the seats are taken!

32
00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.910
I know, I can't wait to
see the look on his face

33
00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.110
when the judge lets him off!

34
00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.430
What a trip! Wow, can't believe
it's been fourteen years.

35
00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:37.140
The ship's under attack!

36
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.370
Get away from it!

37
00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.910
Run! Hurry!

38
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.510
What the?!
Is this a pirate raid?!

39
00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.820
But how? Where is this
attack even coming from?

40
00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.580
Hey, look over there!

41
00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.490
What? Some kind of fleet!

42
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.430
Those look like battleships!

43
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.400
Those pirates are attacking us!

44
00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.370
There's so many of them!
Are they all working together?

45
00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.200
Everybody! Run!

46
00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.410
Get outta the harbor!

47
00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.380
Hurry!

48
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.450
It's not safe near the water!

49
00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.220
My baby! Where's my baby?!

50
00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.600
What's happening?

51
00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:48.730
Who the hell? Who's doing this?!
Who took my ships?

52
00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.730
Tom! We're in trouble!

53
00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.080
Franky's ships are
attacking the harbor!

54
00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.760
It's not him. I saw him earlier.
He wouldn't do such a thing!

55
00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.870
I know that! Look, I'm positive
it's not Franky doing it.

56
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.740
This is a whole other
kind of trouble we're in!

57
00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.840
Let's put a stop to it!

58
00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.580
Right!

59
00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.650
Pirates? Or worse,
the Government.

60
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:13.840
Evacuate!

61
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.970
Hurry! Into the city!

62
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.700
Get away from the harbor!

63
00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.380
My father's still inside!

64
00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.910
Bastards! They're gonna pay!

65
00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:32.050
Who the hell is it, huh?!

66
00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.250
Who the hell is screwing
around with my ships?!

67
00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.690
Please, come with us your honor!
The ship can't take much more!

68
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.970
Who does that fleet belong to?

69
00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.460
The raid on the Judicial Ship
was a success sir.

70
00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.500
Excellent. Now, I want you to
proceed to step two immediately.

71
00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.850
We must ensure that justice is served.

72
00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.350
Yes, sir!

73
00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:09.430
Now, let's begin your impending
trial in earnest. Shall we, Tom?

74
00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.660
It looks like it's about to go down.

75
00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.500
Alright! Let's get back
to Scrap Heap Island.

76
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.640
Right!

77
00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.090
Hey. The fleet is
starting to turn around!

78
00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.270
Hold on.

79
00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.350
I'm pretty sure I've seen
those ships somewhere before!

80
00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:37.020
Tom, look!
They're heading this way!

81
00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.030
They're getting closer!
I think that we can catch 'em!

82
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.150
I can't imagine what the
hell they were thinkin'

83
00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:46.480
pullin' a stunt like that!

84
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.130
I see two men
approaching from the island!

85
00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:53.330
That's Tom. Right!
Let's abandon this ship!

86
00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.890
What the?!
Not a soul on this thing!

87
00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.300
Same here! I don't see anybody!

88
00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:11.670
What the hell is going on here?

89
00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.240
More of Franky's ships?

90
00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.430
Iceburg! Watch out!

91
00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:33.780
Dammit! My Battle Frankies!
They're destroyed!

92
00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:46.840
Tom! Iceburg! Hey!
Can you hear me?!

93
00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:50.300
Are you okay?! What in
the hell happened here?!

94
00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.210
Tell me what's
going on. Hey! Ice...

95
00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:03.780
You stupid ass!

96
00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:13.120
It's your fault this happened.
It was that intelligence agent.

97
00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.530
He used your damn battleships
to attack people at the harbor.

98
00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:21.400
No I-I didn't hurt anybody.

99
00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:25.440
I told you this would happen.
But you don't listen.

100
00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.180
Listen, Franky!

101
00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.390
If you killed a Sea King with this ship,

102
00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.490
then it's a dangerous weapon.

103
00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:32.660
You're making it
easier for somebody

104
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:35.320
who wants to use it
like one, you idiot!

105
00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.830
My ships did this.
They hurt Tom!

106
00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:45.420
Look. We have the ability to
create powerful things, weapons.

107
00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.580
Even if you weren't trying to.

108
00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:51.790
Weapons are made to hurt people.

109
00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:56.530
Whether you want them to or not,
they can hurt your friends.

110
00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.530
That's what the
government did to us.

111
00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.400
They used your creations
to hurt a lot of people.

112
00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.270
People we care about!

113
00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.800
And now they're gonna
put the blame on us.

114
00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.740
They want to back
Tom into a corner

115
00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.240
so they can get
those blueprints.

116
00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:13.950
You still think your hands
don't have blood on them?!

117
00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:18.520
If Tom gets taken away.
If he hangs for this.

118
00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:23.660
I swear on my life.
I will never forgive you!

119
00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:29.680
Never! You unders...

120
00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.450
Stop it!

121
00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.020
Tom!

122
00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:36.150
It's not his fault,
don't blame him.

123
00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:38.360
He didn't do this.

124
00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.760
You still believe that, after
everything that happened?!

125
00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:44.130
Oh, no...

126
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:47.330
This is... This is one of
the special harpoons I made!

127
00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.730
Once it pierces its target, you can't pull
it out!

128
00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.300
I'm so sorry!

129
00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.640
Haha. Don't apologize!

130
00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.370
It's barely even
a scratch! Heh.

131
00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.400
Over there! We found them!

132
00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.900
Tom's been injured!

133
00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.500
Wait, why is he hurt?

134
00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.430
Weren't they the ones behind the attack?

135
00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.470
It doesn't make any sense!

136
00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.120
The townspeople, they're here.

137
00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.540
Now then.

138
00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.590
I believe this is the part
where you come along quietly.

139
00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.320
Damn you, Spanda!

140
00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.290
Spandam, you fool.

141
00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:23.430
Now let's get going, you criminals.

142
00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:28.060
These are the culprits behind the attack!

143
00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:29.190
Rest easy, everyone!

144
00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:33.160
We, the men of CP5, have
destroyed their attack ships.

145
00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.540
They'll cause
no more trouble.

146
00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.200
I'm sure the judge would
have acquitted him

147
00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.950
of those old charges today.

148
00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:42.250
If so, then why did he do something like
that?

149
00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:43.930
He was friends with the King of the
Pirates.

150
00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.580
Who knows what he's capable of?

151
00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.880
Pleased to meet you,
your honor.

152
00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.550
My name is Spandam.
I'm with CP5.

153
00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:53.700
A pleasure.
And thanks, you saved us.

154
00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.000
We can take over the
investigation from here,

155
00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:56.920
if you don't mind.

156
00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.330
We'll give them a full interrogation.

157
00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:02.720
Just try talking your way out of this one.

158
00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.490
The trust they had in you has been
shattered.

159
00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:09.610
Soon, those blueprints for the
ancient weapon will be mine!

160
00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.400
– Gerro, gerro!
– How could this happen?

161
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:20.140
First off, about the Sea Train.
Magnificent work.

162
00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:23.640
With its help, Water Seven will continue to
grow and flourish.

163
00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.640
For that, on the previous charge
of building Gold Roger's ship,

164
00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:30.340
your acquittal today had pretty
much already been decided.

165
00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:32.480
Knowing that, why in the
world would you commit

166
00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.120
such a heinous crime
and erase that opportunity?

167
00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.310
Please, explain yourself.

168
00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:37.480
That's a lie!

169
00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.180
It wasn't Tom or any of us
that attacked the Judicial Ship!

170
00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.670
It was that
idiot, Spandam!

171
00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.550
He's the one responsible!

172
00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:51.950
Sure it was!

173
00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.280
He's not serious, is he?

174
00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.340
What kind of crap is he trying to pull?

175
00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:59.780
Why would a government agency
like CP5 attack a Judicial Ship?

176
00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:00.810
There's no way!

177
00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:03.150
You're gonna have to
come up with a better lie

178
00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.350
than that, Mr. Apprentice.

179
00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.490
Hahahah! Your name is
Cutty Flam, correct?

180
00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.640
I believe that was the name
we took down from you

181
00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:11.600
when we caught you red handed

182
00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:14.470
on board one of those
treacherous raid ships.

183
00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:16.210
And correct me if
I'm mistaken,

184
00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:18.210
but weren't those
very same raid ships

185
00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:20.480
all made by your company?

186
00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.930
Ships that would do
such a horrible thing.

187
00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:34.270
Something so awful,

188
00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:37.400
are no longer my ships!

189
00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.680
Tom tore off his chains!
He's on a rampage!

190
00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.420
Take aim!

191
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:57.010
He just hit him.
Tom has never hit Franky before.

192
00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.560
What'd you do that for?!

193
00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:04.920
They are no longer
your ships, huh?

194
00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.660
Don't you ever say that again!

195
00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.130
What's wrong with saying that?!
I wish I'd never made them!

196
00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.630
If those ships didn't exist,

197
00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:16.530
then nobody would
have gotten hurt!

198
00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:25.010
When a ship is built,
no matter what type

199
00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:27.210
it's neither good nor evil.

200
00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.940
I don't care what kind of ships

201
00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:32.110
you choose to make for
the rest of your life.

202
00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:36.030
Remember, even if the ships
you build hurt someone,

203
00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.400
even if they destroy the world.

204
00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.660
Even if no one else does,

205
00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.250
their creator must love
them unconditionally.

206
00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.090
The one who made them must never deny
them!

207
00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.630
Don't place the blame on the ships!

208
00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.300
You must be proud.

209
00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:52.340
Of every ship
you've ever created!

210
00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.320
Iceburg.

211
00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.330
Franky.

212
00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.290
Whatever happens,

213
00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.400
don't interfere with
what I'm about to do.

214
00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:19.920
No matter what.

215
00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:24.940
It's the World Government
who pinned this crime on us,

216
00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:26.080
and it's the World Government

217
00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.960
There's no way for us to be
cleared of these charges.

218
00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:32.220
It's over.

219
00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.550
It must be tough for you to see
your innocent ships being used

220
00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:37.850
for something as
horrible as this.

221
00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.920
I bet you really wanna hit
that guy, don't you, Franky?

222
00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:52.860
What are you doing?!

223
00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.360
He's going crazy again!

224
00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:55.870
Gerro!

225
00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:56.870
What is he doing?!

226
00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:57.930
Stop it, please!

227
00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:00.440
You're making things worse than they
already are!

228
00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.950
Can you even comprehend the pain

229
00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.390
that you've put
that boy through?!

230
00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.910
Fire!

231
00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.890
They shot him!

232
00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:22.080
Tom, no!

233
00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:31.000
Tranquillizers, huh?

234
00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:35.360
Not so tough now, are you?!
Serves you right, fishman!

235
00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.960
Tom! Wait!
Why are you doing this?!

236
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.570
What are you standing around for?

237
00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.400
Get over there and apprehend them!

238
00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.400
We're going to take Tom
and every last one

239
00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.240
of his villainous workers
down to Enies Lobby!

240
00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.080
Who would have thought that Tom could be
such a dangerous guy?

241
00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.540
What the hell was he thinking?

242
00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:52.960
Just what you'd you expect from

243
00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.970
a man who sold his
soul to pirates!

244
00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.040
He made those battleships and

245
00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:58.980
waited around for a chance
like this to use them!

246
00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:01.740
How dare you talk about him
like that, you bastards!

247
00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.410
Stop it.

248
00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.510
It's all right.

249
00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:06.680
But, Tom!

250
00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:09.350
I'd like to confess.

251
00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:13.320
The raid on the Judicial
Ship was led by me.

252
00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:16.730
That's not true!
Why would you say that?!

253
00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.020
But I have a request.

254
00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:20.620
Save your breath, fishman!

255
00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.000
Nobody gives a
damn about your...!

256
00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.340
Shut your mouth, CP5!

257
00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.310
So, what is this request?

258
00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:30.080
If building the sea train was
supposed to be considered

259
00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.610
a pardon for one
charge against me.

260
00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:36.780
Then I'd like to be pardoned
for today's charges.

261
00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:38.420
Even if that request
is granted,

262
00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:41.090
you'll be right back to where
you were to begin with.

263
00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:44.300
With a charge of building a ship
for the King of the Pirates,

264
00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.870
which will result
in the maximum penalty.

265
00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:47.570
Sounds good.

266
00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:48.810
I like that better, anyway.

267
00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:52.750
Giving a hand to that Roger guy is
something I'll never forget.

268
00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:56.750
In fact, it's something I take great pride
in!

269
00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:00.190
He's proud of that?

270
00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.120
I can't believe he'd
make such a bold claim

271
00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.730
about something so despicable!

272
00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:04.660
Traitor!

273
00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.700
Evil Fishman!

274
00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.290
You'll regret that!

275
00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:09.730
Why, Tom? Tell me!

276
00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.300
It's for the best.

277
00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.930
Now listen, don't
blame yourself for this.

278
00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.830
I never thought the
World Government would go

279
00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:20.760
to such extremes to
get the blueprints.

280
00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:24.140
And the situation with Roger only makes
the matter worse.

281
00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:26.240
Even so, it doesn't have to be this way!

282
00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.540
No, it's fine.

283
00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:28.710
Look around you.

284
00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:32.010
Even if I'm charged with
a crime from 14 years ago,

285
00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.780
nothing else about this town

286
00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.970
is the same now as
it was back then.

287
00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:38.750
This island is alive and strong!

288
00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.620
This is only the beginning.

289
00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:43.630
No matter what ends up
happening to me,

290
00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:47.660
I was still able
to help this town.

291
00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:55.530
My dream has
finally begun to run.

292
00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:57.630
Tom! Don't! Please!

293
00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:00.430
Tom, no!

294
00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.110
Iceburg, Franky take care of
the blueprints.

295
00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:17.880
Kokoro, Yokozuna thank you
for everything.

296
00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:23.870
The tranquilizers finally kicked in!

297
00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:26.570
Capture those three for
the Judicial Ship attack!

298
00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:27.900
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

299
00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.470
Hold it!

300
00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.210
I'm amending the charges.

301
00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:36.130
For the crime of designing
and building a ship

302
00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.180
for Gold Roger, the
King of the Pirates.

303
00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.510
Tom and Tom alone
will be apprehended

304
00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.610
and taken to Enies Lobby.

305
00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:43.720
That is all.

306
00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.820
What in the hell got into that old
geezer's head?

307
00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.440
Whatever, I don't
need his lackeys.

308
00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:54.780
Release those two apprentices!

309
00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.340
Tom can't be saved from this.

310
00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.210
It's the government we're up against.

311
00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:09.110
There's nothing we
can do! Endure it.

312
00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.760
Tom traded his life for yours!

313
00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:14.780
If you make them your enemy,
you won't be able to win,

314
00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.780
no matter how many lives
you have to give!

315
00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:21.030
Enies Lobby is the government's personal
judicial island.

316
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.600
Not one single person who's been

317
00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:28.210
sent to that dreadful place
has ever been seen again!

318
00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:30.310
The sea train is ready for departure,
sir!

319
00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:32.080
We can leave
anytime you like!

320
00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.010
Very good!

321
00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.360
Kokoro.

322
00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:38.990
Let's get moving, men!
Load up the prisoner!

323
00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.040
I can't...

324
00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:44.200
This bloated fishman is
going for a little train ride!

325
00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:46.440
Endure this!

326
00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:49.920
Hey!

327
00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.690
Stop it!

328
00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:06.500
Whoa! He really
messed up his face!

329
00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:10.470
Now Tom's apprentice is the one on a
rampage!

330
00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:11.070
No! Stop!

331
00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:12.340
Gerro, gerro, gerro!

332
00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:13.580
Capture that criminal!

333
00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:16.520
The rest of you, take Tom to the train!

334
00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.920
That's not gonna happen!

335
00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:20.120
Nobody's taking him anywhere!

336
00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.320
Fire at will!

337
00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:25.090
Tom's staying right here!

338
00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:29.010
Are you okay?!

339
00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.240
After him!

340
00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:33.240
Hurry! Get out of here!

341
00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:34.400
Fire!

342
00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:47.730
Dammit! He got away!

343
00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:51.320
I'll get that Cutty Flam brat if it's the
last thing I do!

344
00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.650
That little criminal will pay for what
he's done!

345
00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:54.890
Mark my words.

346
00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:58.350
Once this case is over, I'll
have him sent to the gallows!

347
00:20:58.380 --> 00:20:59.480
Spandam! He's here!

348
00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:00.470
What now?!

349
00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:03.100
It's-It's Cutty
Flam, sir!

350
00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:04.000
What?! Where?

351
00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.170
Standing out on the tracks ahead of us!

352
00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:09.240
And it appears that he's holding some sort
of weapon!

353
00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:15.560
Stay right there, Yokozuna.

354
00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.650
Gerro, gerro.

355
00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.420
He's out of his mind!

356
00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:20.700
What should we do, sir?

357
00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:23.100
Are you out of
your mind, too?!

358
00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:24.570
We keep on going!

359
00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.170
That's what he wants us to do,
right?

360
00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:27.810
Don't worry about him!

361
00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.140
Right! Y-Yes, sir!

362
00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:34.180
All right, Puffing Tom.
That's far enough!

363
00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:38.050
What do you think you're doing?

364
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.280
Where are you taking your creator?

365
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.710
Gerro, gerro, gerro!

366
00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:54.750
I won't let you pass!

367
00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:04.050
Give me Tom back!

368
00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:07.080
You hear me?

369
00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:09.980
You hear me?!
Stop now, sea train!

370
00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:08.680
Stop now, C.J.!

371
00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:14.730
I see!

372
00:22:14.780 --> 00:22:16.820
So your parents just abandoned you,
huh?

373
00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:18.500
That's terrible!

374
00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:20.230
Hey! Stop laughing at me!

375
00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:23.070
Fine then.
Come stay with me.

376
00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:25.280
Tom.

377
00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:27.220
I don't want to build ships anymore.

378
00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:32.560
I can't love ships that hurt the
people I care so much about!

379
00:22:32.590 --> 00:22:35.060
I won't do it!

380
00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:40.860
But even so, my goal in
life is to be just like you!

381
00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:51.380
Come back!

382
00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:55.610
Come back and
teach me once again!

383
00:23:03.850 --> 00:23:08.520
Cause someday I want to
build my own dream ship!

384
00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:16.200
A ship that will proudly
sail bravely over

385
00:23:16.230 --> 00:23:20.970
uncharted waters all the way
to the ends of the world!
